From fb227e208b2d1f25a37b07da965473062a27fa1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Offer a sheet style for the tabs drawer, behind a setting.

Settings > Appearance > Address bar & toolbar now has a Tabs style
choice. Side drawer is the default and keeps the existing drawer. Sheet
opens the same list from the Vertical tabs button, laid out as a sheet
above the real bottom toolbar: a handle and the current tab's domain at
the top, and the tab count, list/grid, new tab, and close-all actions
at the bottom of the sheet. The address bar and the five toolbar
buttons stay visible and tappable.

The sheet reuses the drawer's RecyclerView, adapter, drag-reorder,
swipe-to-close, list/grid, and pinned-group rules. Glass blur is off in
sheet mode so it does not cover the toolbar. With the address bar on
top, the sheet fills the gap between the two bars; a full visual mirror
is a later step.

Tested on the Android emulator (Pixel 10 Pro profile).
